  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Sudasi (whose name means based on the number \"six\") is a very popular iqa‘ to accompany folk line dances from Lebanon and Palestine, like the Dabke. It can modulate to 3 back-to-back measures of Iqa‘ Malfuf.",
    "An alternative form of Iqa‘ Sudasi starts with 3 consecutive dum-s, and is commonly used in Lebanese dabke songs."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Sudasi 6/4 Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Sudasi Iqa‘ Sudasi (whose name means based on the number \"six\") is a very popular iqa‘ to accompany folk line dances from Lebanon and Palestine, like the Dabke. It can modulate to 3 back-to-back measures of Iqa‘ Malfuf . Dal‘ona Fairouz (traditional Lebanese folk song) Ya Mahla Layali el-Hawa (1963) Fairouz Music and lyrics by the Rahbani Brothers Ya Hajal Sannin (1965) Fairouz Music and lyrics by the Rahbani Brothers From the movie Bayya‘ el-Khawatim Iqa‘ Sudasi 6/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan The second form of Iqa‘ Sudasi An alternative form of Iqa‘ Sudasi starts with 3 consecutive dum -s, and is commonly used in Lebanese dabke songs. Ya Trab ‘Ayntura Fairouz, Wadih al-Safi and Nasri Shamseddine Music and lyrics by the Rahbani Brothers Ya Ba‘albak Music and lyrics by Tania Saleh",
